nodes.body:
Addressed the P2 support-query mismatch in `768d4462`. Both `SparseIndexerScoreRecompute.check_support()` and `SparseAttnScoreRecompute.check_support()` now reuse the exact prepared-compiler capacity guard on SM90 only; SM100 admission remains unchanged.

Validation on H200: the new regression was RED before the fix (4/4 invalid-width cases failed to raise), then GREEN after the fix (8/8 SM90-rejection and SM100-preservation cases passed). The full affected L0/L1 file passed with **43 passed, 26 skipped**; changed-file pre-commit, `py_compile`, and `git diff --check` also passed. No device code, compile key, execution path, synchronization, workspace, or CUDA Graph behavior changed.

@coderabbitai review

